# Docs and evidence

## Docs
- Plain, short, task-oriented. Reference files and commands instead of copying code that will drift.
- Docs describe what exists; mark planned work as planned. Never document a command that does not run.
- Architecture lives in `docs/architecture/` (domain, ledger, API, state machines, authorization and DoA matrix); decisions as ADRs in `docs/adr/NNNN-title.md` (context, decision, consequences). A change that contradicts an ADR adds a new ADR.
- UX specs live in `docs/ux/screens/NNN-slug.md`.
- Public repo: fictional data only; no internal company content, URLs, ticket keys or names.
- `AGENTS.md` files stay under about 80 lines; detail belongs in rules or skills. Area templates live in `docs/ai-harness/agents-md/`.

## Evidence packs
```text
evidence/<phase-id>/
  README.md        gate review (template: phase-gate-review skill)
  gate-summary.txt scripts/gate.sh --evidence output
  <change>/functional/  /functional-check: outcome table, screenshots, API responses, log excerpts
  visual-qa/       /visual-qa: report.md, report.json, screens/, design-parity/, before-after/
  api/             scrubbed request/response samples for the phase's key flows
  db/              scrubbed query results proving invariants (balances, rebuild check, RLS)
  perf/            autocannon results when the gate asks
```
- Raw traces, videos, HAR files, compose logs and DB dumps stay in `tmp/evidence/` (gitignored); they contain tokens and personal data. Only scrubbed summaries are committed.
- Every claim in an evidence README points to a file or command output. Capture with `/functional-check` and `/visual-qa`, assemble with `/phase-review`.
